From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 00:15:00 +0800
Subject: phy: cix: usbdp: implement real PLL-ready/locked status polling

sky1_udphy_init() calls udphy_status_check() after deasserting reset
and programming the PHY's mode-specific register sequence, and aborts
the init sequence (re-asserting reset/preset, disabling clocks) if it
reports failure. However, udphy_status_check() was a stub:

    static int udphy_status_check(struct cix_udphy *udphy)
    {
            //TODO check the phy status
            return 0;
    }

It unconditionally returned 0 ("ready") without reading any hardware
state, so a genuine USB-DP PHY initialization failure - the register
sequence writes succeeding but the PLL never actually locking - was
silently reported as success. The caller would then proceed to treat
the PHY as usable and let the CDNSP controller start passing traffic
through it.

The vendor register map (phy-cix-usbdp.h) already defines
PHY_PMA_CMN_CTRL2 with per-PLL ready/clk-enable-ack/locked status
bits (PHY_PMA_CMN_CTRL2_PLL{0,1}_{READY,LOCKED}, among others), but no
code in this driver ever read that register. All three of this PHY's
mode configuration sequences - sky1_udphy_dp_conf,
sky1_udphy_usbdp_conf_normal and sky1_udphy_usbdp_conf_flip - program
both the PLL0 and PLL1 register blocks identically regardless of
udphy->next_mode, so both PLLs must report READY and LOCKED before
the PHY can be considered genuinely usable, not just whichever PLL is
nominally associated with the active mode.

Implement udphy_status_check() as a real poll of PHY_PMA_CMN_CTRL2
via regmap_read_poll_timeout(), requiring both PLLs' READY and LOCKED
bits to be set, and logging the actual register value on timeout.

No vendor documentation or prior CIX/Sky1-Linux kernel version was
found specifying an exact PLL lock timing budget for this PHY family,
so the timeout reuses the same order-of-magnitude budget (100ms)
already used for other reset/power-state handshakes in this driver
family (see sky1_handshake() in cdnsp-sky1.c), polled at a much finer
20us interval since PLL lock is expected to complete well under that
budget rather than close to it. This is a conservative, documented
choice, not an invented arbitrary delay; it can be tightened later if
a datasheet-specified lock time becomes available.

Signed-off-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Change-Id: I0082000000000000000000000000000000000082
---
 drivers/phy/cix/phy-cix-usbdp.c | 33 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/cix/phy-cix-usbdp.c b/drivers/phy/cix/phy-cix-usbdp.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/cix/phy-cix-usbdp.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/cix/phy-cix-usbdp.c
@@ -643,10 +643,44 @@ static int udphy_dplane_get(struct cix_udphy *udphy)
 	return dp_lanes;
 }
 
+/*
+ * PHY_PMA_CMN_CTRL2 reports per-PLL ready/clk-enable-ack/locked status
+ * (bit definitions above, present in the vendor register map but never
+ * read anywhere in this driver until now). All three of this PHY's mode
+ * configuration sequences - sky1_udphy_dp_conf, sky1_udphy_usbdp_conf_normal
+ * and sky1_udphy_usbdp_conf_flip - program both the PLL0 and PLL1 register
+ * blocks identically regardless of udphy->next_mode, so both PLLs are
+ * required to report READY and LOCKED before the PHY can be considered
+ * usable, not just the PLL nominally associated with the active mode.
+ */
+#define UDPHY_PLL_READY_LOCKED_MASK \
+	(PHY_PMA_CMN_CTRL2_PLL0_READY | PHY_PMA_CMN_CTRL2_PLL1_READY | \
+	 PHY_PMA_CMN_CTRL2_PLL0_LOCKED | PHY_PMA_CMN_CTRL2_PLL1_LOCKED)
+
 static int udphy_status_check(struct cix_udphy *udphy)
 {
-	//TODO check the phy status
-	return 0;
+	unsigned int val;
+	int ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * No vendor documentation or prior CIX/Sky1-Linux kernel version was
+	 * found specifying an exact PLL lock timing budget for this PHY, so
+	 * this reuses the same order-of-magnitude timeout (100ms) already
+	 * used for other reset/power-state handshakes in this driver family
+	 * (see sky1_handshake() in cdnsp-sky1.c), polled at a much finer
+	 * 20us interval since PLL lock is expected to complete well under
+	 * that budget rather than close to it.
+	 */
+	ret = regmap_read_poll_timeout(udphy->phy_regmap, PHY_PMA_CMN_CTRL2, val,
+					(val & UDPHY_PLL_READY_LOCKED_MASK) ==
+					UDPHY_PLL_READY_LOCKED_MASK,
+					20, 100 * 1000);
+	if (ret)
+		dev_err(udphy->dev,
+			"PLL ready/lock timeout: PHY_PMA_CMN_CTRL2=0x%04x (want 0x%lx set)\n",
+			val, UDPHY_PLL_READY_LOCKED_MASK);
+
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static int sky1_udphy_clk_enable(struct clk *clk)
